% The program of stats-exists.dl planned without existence checks.  Each
% p(_, X) after the first is a lookup of X matching both tuples of p, so the
% rule derives s(x) twice for every binding that reaches it: eight times,
% the two tuples of the first literal doubled by each of the two lookups,
% where the checks derive it twice.  The query derives its row once either
% way, and every other count but the reads is the same.

p(a, x).
p(b, x).

s(X) :- p(_, X), p(_, X), p(_, X).

s(X)?
